# Always use agent-brain when useful

## Knowledge (durable experience)

When you learn a reusable solution, procedure, or expertise in this session:

1. Store it via agent-brain HTTP API (`POST /api/v1/knowledge`) with the right `kind`.
2. All knowledge is stored in SQLite (`store_target: sqlite`).
3. Before solving a familiar problem, call `POST /api/v1/knowledge/search` (structured) first.

## Sessions (Cursor chats)

Cursor session telemetry (context %, tokens, thinking, turns) lives in
SQLite tables `sessions` / `turns` under the WebUI **Sessions** section.
Fill via Windows `agent-brain-dispatcher sync` / `ingest`, or MCP
`list_sessions` to browse — not knowledge endpoints.

Do not confuse knowledge APIs with session tools. Do not use
centralized-agent-data for new work — agent-brain owns both surfaces.
